#%PAM-1.0
# buchhwin-shell lock screen (lock.qml) on Arch Linux. system-auth is the
# stack every login includes there (system-login, sudo, polkit), so the
# fingerprint reader does not go into it: SDDM and sudo would wait for a
# finger first, and a finger login cannot open KWallet or gnome-keyring.
# It goes here, as `auth sufficient pam_fprintd.so` directly above the
# include - Settings > Lock Screen shows the command, and the user decides.
# buchhwin-lock-password stays password-only. pam_faillock in system-auth
# counts wrong passwords here as at any login.
auth       include      system-auth
account    required     pam_permit.so
